  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Banking &amp; Financial Services - Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to assist the GoE in developing and maintaining a fair, safe, and stable financial sector that benefits and protects financial sector participants while maintaining public confidence in the financial system and supporting private sector-led economic growth. Project components will focus on: (1) enhancing the financial sector legal and regulatory framework to improve NBE oversight; (2) strengthening the capacity of NBE banking supervision and microfinance institution supervision staff to adequately regulate and supervise the banking and NBFI sectors; (3) establishing a deposit insurance regime that protects depositors in the event of bank failures and maintains public confidence in the financial sector; (4) developing and implementing an effective resolution framework that allows for the orderly resolution of failed financial institutions; (5) developing and implementing a crisis management framework; (6) enhancing the NBE&apos;s capacity to monitor and react to macroprudential risks to financial sector stability; (7) strengthening the capacity of NBE insurance supervision staff to adequately regulate and supervise the insurance sector; and (8) en</narrative>
  </description>
